# {{.Name}}

A [browserscale.cloud](https://browserscale.cloud) automation module, scaffolded
with `browserscale init`. Built on the **browserscale-kit** harness (config,
store, logging) and the **browserscale-go** SDK (cloud browser control).

{{- if or (eq .Kind "queue") (eq .Kind "one-shot")}}
`register.go` ships with a **complete, working example flow** against the
browserscale playground — run it first to see the whole shape, then replace
that body with your own registration. `flow.go` only dispatches to it; add
further flows as sibling files (`enter.go`, `login.go`, …).
{{- else}}
`task.go` ships with a **complete, working example flow** against the
browserscale playground — run it first to see the whole shape, then replace
that body with your own task. `flow.go` only dispatches to it; split into
named flow files (`register.go`, `enter.go`, …) as the module grows.
{{- end}}

## Run

```bash
go mod tidy
go run .
```

`go run .` opens the configurator: fill in the config (saved to
`data/config.json`), pick a run name, and the module runs. Outputs land in
`runs/<name>/`. Next time your saved config is pre-loaded — just press Continue.

**Every run is proxied.** Add at least one proxy to `data/proxies.txt`
(see the comments in that file for the accepted formats) — the run refuses to
start without one.
{{if eq .Kind "queue"}}
This module registers each account from a **CSV**: a ready-to-run sample lives
at `data/accounts.csv` (header `email,firstname,lastname,password,country`).
The configurator verifies the file parses and every row has all five columns
before saving.

The example flow targets the public
[playground](https://browserscale.cloud/playground/registration_flow) — a
deliberately hostile signup fixture (cookie wall in a cross-origin iframe behind
a closed shadow root, a timed newsletter modal, a submit button in its own
closed shadow root, an emailed verification code). Besides proxies it needs a
**catch-all mailbox** (IMAP host/port/user/pass) that receives the codes — each
row's `email` must be an address on that domain.
{{else if eq .Kind "one-shot"}}
The example flow registers a single account against the public
[playground](https://browserscale.cloud/playground/registration_flow) — a
deliberately hostile signup fixture (cookie wall in a cross-origin iframe behind
a closed shadow root, a timed newsletter modal, a submit button in its own
closed shadow root, an emailed verification code). The account and its
**catch-all mailbox** (IMAP) are plain consts at the top of `register.go` —
edit them and run.
{{end}}
After `data/config.json` exists, iterate headless:

```bash
browserscale dev              # rebuild → restart → stream (timestamp under runs/)
browserscale dev -run nightly # same, fixed runs/nightly/
```

## Layout

| Path            | What it's for                                                      |
|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `flow.go`       | Thin dispatcher — `doTask()` picks which named flow to run         |
{{- if or (eq .Kind "queue") (eq .Kind "one-shot")}}
| `register.go`   | **Your main job** — one named flow (worked playground signup)      |
{{- else}}
| `task.go`       | **Your main job** — one named flow (worked playground example)     |
{{- end}}
| `module.go`     | Identity + config schema (`Schema()`), edited via the configurator |
| `run.go`        | The `{{.Kind}}` lifecycle (workers, loop, scheduling) — editable   |
| `rent.go`       | Proxy loading + rent-with-backoff helper (`loadProxies`, `rent`)   |
| `main.go`       | Hands off to the kit harness                                       |
| `AGENTS.md`     | SDK + kit reference and patterns for your code agent               |
| `data/`         | `config.json`, input files (`proxies.txt`, …), `store.db`          |
| `runs/<name>/`  | Per-run outputs (`registered.txt`, …)                              |

Add further browser flows as sibling files (`enter.go`, `login.go`, …) — one
named flow per file — and keep `doTask` as the switchboard.

## Config

The config is defined in `module.go` (`Schema()`), edited in the TUI, and
saved as **`data/config.json`**. It starts with:

- **Browserscale API key** (required)
- **Proxies** — a proxy list under `data/` (required; every run is proxied)
{{- if eq .Kind "queue"}}
- **Accounts CSV** — `email,firstname,lastname,password,country` per row, under `data/` (verified on save)
- **IMAP host/port/user/pass** — the catch-all mailbox the codes land in
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .Threading "configurable"}}
- **Threads** — number of concurrent workers
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .Kind "repeat"}}
- **Amount** — successful runs before stopping
{{- end}}
{{- if eq .Kind "scheduled"}}
- **Interval (seconds)** — seconds between runs
{{- end}}

Add your own fields (input lists, proxies, toggles) by extending `Config` and
`Schema()`.
